{
 "description": "Virtual time, symmetric P2P: the consumer probes k1, which the producer pins; 20 s later it probes k2 in the same round, also pinned. At 30 s k1's pin times out (_STORE_TIMEOUT_S) and is withdrawn from the round's supply. The consumer's fetch then demands k1 and k2: the round's supply cannot meet k1, and since a symmetric round's supply precedes its fetch, the producer fails the round at once (TransferDone(success=False)), so the consumer's load fails now, not at its load timeout.",
